From 7b89ac411091fb4d0de9fd21fc8d71be5acfb889 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex6357 <73743056+Alex6357@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 20:59:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] optional: revert rc.subr MFC r351863 ${name}_env export
 (abf14b58ac7) [CONFLICT POINT]

This is a CONFLICT POINT decision: 15.1 upstream retains MFC r351863
(rc.subr honors ${name}_env when a custom *_cmd is defined, exporting
it via 'eval "export -- $_env"'). TrueNAS reverted it (abf14b58ac7,
ryan@ixsystems) because ix-* rc scripts do their own env handling and
the 'export -- $_env' sh-builtin has variable-name limitations that
break them.

Rebase decision: KEEP the TrueNAS revert (both call sites).
15.1 added a second export site in the _offcmd branch (line ~1743) that
did not exist at 13.3; this rebase reverts BOTH sites (1365-1367 and
1742-1744) to fully honor the TrueNAS intent of 'rc.subr does not auto-
export ${name}_env'. The surrounding 15.1 run_rc_command additions
(rc_trace, svcj jailing, _run_rc_setup/_run_rc_precmd refactor) are all
preserved -- only the two 3-line export blocks are removed.

rc.subr.8: drop the paragraph documenting the export limitation.

Reviewers who prefer upstream behavior can skip this patch and instead
adapt ix-* rc scripts to the upstream export semantics.
---
 libexec/rc/rc.subr       |  6 ------
 share/man/man8/rc.subr.8 | 14 ++------------
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libexec/rc/rc.subr b/libexec/rc/rc.subr
index 4e19d10f5e4e..37d0cc923a4e 100644
--- a/libexec/rc/rc.subr
+++ b/libexec/rc/rc.subr
@@ -1362,9 +1362,6 @@ run_rc_command()
 			if [ "$_cmd" != : ]; then
 				rc_trace 1 "$_cmd"
 			fi
-			if [ -n "$_env" ]; then
-				eval "export -- $_env"
-			fi
 
 			if [ "${_rc_svcj}" != jailing ]; then
 				# service can redefine all so
@@ -1739,9 +1736,6 @@ _run_rc_offcmd()
 {
 	eval _offcmd=\$${name}_offcmd
 	if [ -n "$_offcmd" ]; then
-		if [ -n "$_env" ]; then
-			eval "export -- $_env"
-		fi
 		debug "run_rc_command: ${name}_offcmd: $_offcmd $rc_extra_args"
 		eval "$_offcmd $rc_extra_args"
 		_return=$?
diff --git a/share/man/man8/rc.subr.8 b/share/man/man8/rc.subr.8
index 45a9e9a684cd..22e5340706e3 100644
--- a/share/man/man8/rc.subr.8
+++ b/share/man/man8/rc.subr.8
@@ -710,19 +710,9 @@ is mounted.
 A list of environment variables to run
 .Va command
 with.
-Those variables will be passed as arguments to the
+This will be passed as arguments to the
 .Xr env 1
-utility unless
-.Ar argument Ns Va _cmd
-is defined.
-In that case the contents of
-.Va ${name}_env
-will be exported via the
-.Xr export 1
-builtin of
-.Xr sh 1 ,
-which puts some limitations on the names of variables
-(e.g., a variable name may not start with a digit).
+utility.
 .It Va ${name}_env_file
 A file to source for environmental variables to run
 .Va command
